    "body": "## Description\n\nAdd a GitHub Actions workflow that runs a markdown linter on every pull request. This keeps documentation clean and consistent as more contributors join.\n\n## Steps to Complete\n\n1. Create `.github/workflows/markdown-lint.yml`.\n2. Use the `DavidAnson/markdownlint-cli2-action` action to lint all markdown files.\n3. Configure it to run on `push` and `pull_request` to `main`.\n4. Optionally add a `.markdownlint.json` config to relax rules that don't fit the project.\n5. Commit with `ci: add markdown lint workflow`.\n6. Open a pull request.\n\n## Learning Outcomes\n\n- Writing your first GitHub Actions workflow.\n- Understanding how CI runs automatically on pull requests.\n\n## Helpful Resources\n\n- [markdownlint-cli2-action](https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint-cli2-action)\n- [GitHub Actions: Quickstart](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/quickstart)\n",
